   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( y = f(x) \\) be the solution to the differential equation \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = x + y \\) with \\( f(0) = 2 \\). Find the approximation to \\( f(1) \\) given by Euler's method, starting at \\( x = 0 \\) with three steps of equal size. Give the exact value."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         46,
         9
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The step size is \\( \\Delta x = \\frac{1 - (0)}{3} = \\frac{1}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            3
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At \\( (0, 2) \\) the slope is \\( 2 \\), so \\( y \\approx 2 + (\\frac{1}{3})(2) = \\frac{8}{3} \\) at \\( x = \\frac{1}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            8,
            3
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At \\( (\\frac{1}{3}, \\frac{8}{3}) \\) the slope is \\( 3 \\), so \\( y \\approx \\frac{8}{3} + (\\frac{1}{3})(3) = \\frac{11}{3} \\) at \\( x = \\frac{2}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            11,
            3
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "At \\( (\\frac{2}{3}, \\frac{11}{3}) \\) the slope is \\( \\frac{13}{3} \\), so \\( y \\approx \\frac{11}{3} + (\\frac{1}{3})(\\frac{13}{3}) = \\frac{46}{9} \\) at \\( x = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            46,
            9
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 5,
         "text": "So \\( f(1) \\approx \\frac{46}{9} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            46,
            9
         ]
      }
   ],
